course: dictionary
lesson: 10461
title: Tsunami: a wave, or a flood of something
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tsunami is a huge sea wave, or a series of waves, caused by an earthquake, volcano or landslide under the sea. «If an earthquake at the coast is long or strong, go to high ground or inland at once, because a tsunami may follow within minutes.» The word tells you the danger is serious, so you must act fast.
explain: Sometimes the warning is the sea itself. «If the sea suddenly pulls far back from the beach, a tsunami may be coming: go to high ground at once.» A sudden drop of the sea is a warning sign, so do not stay to watch it.
explain: The word has a second meaning. A tsunami can also be a huge amount of something arriving at once, like a tsunami of emails. Read the words around it: if they talk about the sea, the coast or earthquakes, it is the wave; if they talk about emails, messages or questions, it is a flood of something.
fact: A tsunami is a huge sea wave, or a series of waves, caused by an earthquake, volcano or landslide under the sea.
fact: «Tsunami» can also mean a huge amount of something arriving at once.
fact: A sudden drop of the sea far back from the shore can be a warning sign of a tsunami.
fact: When there is a warning sign, go to high ground or inland at once.
fact: Tsunami warning centres use earthquake sensors and pressure gauges on the sea floor to warn coasts.
exercise: «The 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami followed a magnitude 9.1 earthquake off Sumatra.» What causes a tsunami? | A strong wind blowing across the sea | Rain falling for a long time | A ship hitting a rock | *An earthquake, volcano or landslide under the sea
exercise: «Often the sea suddenly drains far back from the beach just before a tsunami arrives.» What should you do if you see this? | *Go to high ground at once | Run down to the beach to look for fish | Take a photo and stay on the sand | Swim out to meet the wave
exercise: Ravi says, «My inbox got a tsunami of emails today.» What does tsunami mean here? | A kind of fish | *A huge amount of something arriving at once | A sudden loud noise | A huge wave of water
test: What do tsunami warning centres use to warn coasts? | Lighthouses and foghorns | *Earthquake sensors and pressure gauges on the sea floor | Sirens in the desert | Kites and balloons
test: Mia reads, «If an earthquake at the coast is long or strong, go to high ground or inland at once.» Why should she go? | To take a photo of the earthquake | To find her friends at the shops | *Because a tsunami may follow within minutes | Because the sea is warm
exam: Read: «If the sea suddenly pulls far back from the beach, a tsunami may be coming.» Why is this a reason to act at once? | Tsunamis only happen in winter | The beach is a good place to find shells | Waves always get smaller first | *The sea pulling back is a warning sign of a tsunami
